## Executive summary

The objective of this project is to predict how participants performed a
barbell lift. The outcome, `classe`, contains five categories: A represents the
correct technique, while B through E represent four common mistakes.

I removed administrative fields and variables containing mostly missing values.
I then tuned a random forest using five-fold cross-validation. Model performance
was estimated on a separate validation set that was not used during training.
Finally, the selected model was trained on all available observations and used
to classify the 20 course quiz cases.

